  "topicCode": "1.1",
  "topicName": "EQ1: Why are some locations more at risk from tectonic hazards?",
  "text": "Study Figure 1a in the Resource Booklet and Figure 1b below.\nThis data in Figure 1b was collected to investigate whether there was a significant\ndifference in earthquake depth at the two plate boundaries shown in Figure 1a.\nPlate boundary A Number of Mean focal depth\nearthquakes of earthquakes\nrecorded in 2016 (in kilometres)\n186 34.8\nPlate boundary B 145 12.7\nFigure 1b\nFrequency and focal depth of earthquakes in New Zealand, 2016\n(i) Calculate the average monthly frequency of earthquakes at the two plate\nboundaries.\nYou must show your working.\n(ii) A Student’s t-test was used to determine whether there was a statistical\ndifference in the mean focal depth of the earthquakes at the two plate\nboundaries.\nTwo hypotheses were tested:\nNull Hypothesis: There is no statistically significant difference between the\nmean focal depth of earthquakes at the two plate boundaries.\nAlternative Hypothesis: There is a statistically significant difference between\nthe mean focal depth of earthquakes at the two plate boundaries.\n𝑡𝑡 𝑡 𝑥𝑥$ − 𝑥𝑥&\n𝑆𝑆$& + 𝑆𝑆&&\n𝑁𝑁$ 𝑁𝑁&\nUsing the partially completed Student’s t-test below, calculate the value of t.\nt = 22.1\n4.43\nt= .............................................................\n(iii) Study Figure 1c below.\nConfidence level 0.10 (90% 0.05 (95% 0.01 (99%\nsignificance) significance) significance)\nCritical value of 1.6 2.0 2.6\nStudent’s t-test\nFigure 1c\nCritical values for this Student’s t-test\nUsing the Student’s t-test value calculated in (a) (ii), state whether there is a\nsignificant difference between the mean focal depth of the earthquakes.",
  "ms": "Indicative content Mark number (2)\nAO3 (4 marks)\n(1)\n(1)\n(i) Award 1 mark for the correct working of equation:\n331 12 Award 1 mark for the correct frequency of 27.58 (accept 27.6 or 28 or any other accurate rounding up of 27.5833333).\nIf NO working award 1 mark for frequency of 27.6 Allow for calculations of both plate boundaries separately as follows:\nAward 1 mark for both of the calculations of 186/12 for Plate Boundary A and 145/12 for Plate Boundary B Award 1 mark for both of the frequencies of 15.5 (allow 15.50 or 16) for Plate Boundary A and 12.08 (allow 12.1 or 12 or any other accurate rounding up of 12.0833333) for Plate Boundary B.\n(ii)\nAward 1 mark for the correct value of t alone 4.99 (accept 4.989 or 5 or any other accurate rounding up of 4.98871332).\nNOTE: Allow credit to be given for answers not necessarily placed by the t=……………\n(iii)\nAward 1 mark for rejection of null hypothesis as t value is more than critical value at all confidence levels and the acceptance of the alternative hypothesis that there is a statistically significant difference in the mean focal depth of the earthquakes at the 99% confidence level.\nOR Award 1 mark for agreeing that there is a significant difference between the mean focal depth of the earthquakes.\nOR Award 1 mark stating that there is more than 99% likelihood that there is a significant difference.\nOR Award 1 mark for stating that there is less than 1% likelihood that this difference occurred by chance.",
