  "topicName": null,
  "text": "Explain one impact of an El Niño event on the hydrological system.",
  "ms": "Answer Mark number (3)\nAO1 – 2 marks/AO2 – 1 marks Award 1 AO2 mark for analysing the resource to identify a change in the climate during an El Nino event and a further 2 AO1 marks expansion up to a maximum of 3 marks to explain the impact of the hydrological system. For example:\n• Precipitation levels will drop in north east Brazil during an El Nino event (1). This reduction will lead to lower river flows (1) as well as lower soil moisture levels (1).\n• Precipitation levels will increase in California during an El Nino event (1). This will lead to higher levels of surface runoff (1) - and possibility of flood events as river flow exceeds bankful capacity\n(1).\nAccept other explanations of the impacts of an El Nino event on hydrological system",
  "pageFrom": 20,
  "pageTo": 20,
  "pdf": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 1 (Physical)/Questions/June 2020 QP.pdf",
