  "topicName": "EQ2: How do characteristic coastal landforms contribute to coastal landscapes?",
  "text": "Explain the contribution of erosional processes in producing sediment.\n\nStudy Figure 3b in the Resource Booklet.\n(b) Explain the role of global warming in changing mean sea level since 1920.\n",
  "ms": "number Explain the contribution of erosional processes in producing sediment.\nAO1 (3 marks/AO2 (3 marks)\nAO1 The Sediment Cell concept (sources, transfers and sinks) is important in understanding the coast as a system of dynamic equilibrium, with both negative and positive feedback.\n• The importance of erosion processes (hydraulic action, corrosion, abrasion, attrition) and how they are influenced by wave type, size and lithology.\n• Mass movement (blockfall, rotational slumping, landslides) is important on some coasts with weak and/or complex geology.\n• Wave type\nAO2\n• The diagram shows an idealised sediment cell.\n• There are three main sources shown – erosion, mass movement and movement of beach through destructive waves.\n• Expect details of erosional processes such as hydraulic action, corrosion, abrasion.\n• The question states contribution and so expect:\n• Details of other sources such as mass movement from the cliffs.\n• Details of destructive waves moving sediment from the beach.\n• Details of windblown sand from the beach.\nAccept contributions from off-shore deposits.\nAccept other explanations of the contribution of erosional processes in producing sediment.\nLevel Mark Descriptor 0 No rewardable material.\nLevel Mark Descriptor\nLevel 1 1–2\n• Demonstrates isolated or generic elements of geographical\nLevel 2 3–4 knowledge and understanding, some of which may be inaccurate or irrelevant. (AO1)\nLevel 3 5–6\n• Applies knowledge and understanding to geographical information inconsistently. Connections/relationships between stimulus material and the question may be irrelevant. (AO2)\n• Demonstrates geographical knowledge and understanding, which is mostly relevant and may include some inaccuracies.\n(AO1)\n• Applies knowledge and understanding to geographical information to find some relevant connections/relationships between stimulus material and the question. (AO2)\n• Demonstrates accurate and relevant geographical knowledge and understanding throughout. (AO1)\n• Applies knowledge and understanding to geographical information logically to find fully relevant connections/relationships between stimulus material and the question. (AO2)",
  "pageFrom": 14,
  "pageTo": 15,
  "pdf": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 1 (Physical)/Questions/June 2023 QP.pdf",
  "rb": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 1 (Physical)/Questions/June 2023 QP.pdf",
