  "text": "Study Figure 4 below.\nCountry % of population GDP per capita\nUnited States living overseas (US$)\n0.5 69,287\nSwitzerland 7.4 77,324\nNorway 3.5 79,201\nIreland 17.5 106,455\nNetherlands 4.9 63,766\nMexico 12.2 20,036\nJapan 0.6 43,940\nTurkey 4.4 30,372\nFigure 4\nPercentage of population living overseas and\nGDP per capita for a selection of countries, 2021\n(i) Calculate the mean percentage of population living overseas for the countries\nshown in Figure 4.\nGive your answer to one decimal place.\nYou must show your working.\n\n(ii) Calculate the range in GDP per capita for the countries shown.\nYou must show your working.\nUS$ ..............................................................\n(iii) Study Figure 4.\nSuggest why the percentage of the population living overseas varies for these\ncountries.\n",
