  "eq": "geo4-3",
  "eqConfident": true,
  "topicCode": "4.3",
  "topicName": "EQ3: How is regeneration managed?",
  "text": "Explain how local government policies are used to make their areas attractive for\ninward investment.\n",
  "ms": "Explain how local government policies are used to make their areas attractive for number inward investment.\nAO1 (6 marks)\n• Local governments may develop Science Parks which are aimed at attracting knowledge-based industries. These tend to have purpose-built buildings and infrastructure, as well as networking groups allowing similar industries to develop. E.g. Cambridge Science Park is linked to the university, specialising in life sciences.\n• Areas such as Cornwall have implemented specific Enterprise Zones focused on attracting investors through council business rate discounts, a planning- free environment and the provision of superfast broadband.\n• Often legal agreements between councils and developers are created which are linked to planning permissions. They compel the developer to make a financial contribution towards or provide improvements to mitigate against the impact of their development.\n• Local councils may use sport, art and culture to attract inward investment and provide external funding e.g. Olympic Queen Elizabeth Park, Liverpool Capital of Culture.\n• Some local governments have used their heritage to attract investors focused on tourism. This has been used successfully in the Titanic Quarter in Belfast and Southampton.\nAccept any other appropriate response Level Mark Descriptor\nLevel 1 0 No rewardable material.\nLevel 2 1–2\nLevel 3 • Demonstrates isolated elements of geographical knowledge and 3–4 understanding, some of which may be inaccurate or irrelevant.\n5–6 (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a narrow range of geographical ideas, which lack detail. (AO1)\n• Demonstrates geographical knowledge and understanding, which is mostly relevant and may include some inaccuracies. (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a range of geographical ideas, which are not fully detailed and/or developed. (AO1)\n• Demonstrates accurate and relevant geographical knowledge and understanding throughout. (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a broad range of geographical ideas, which are detailed and fully developed. (AO1)",
  "pageFrom": 10,
  "pageTo": 10,
  "pdf": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 2 (Human)/Questions/June 2024 QP.pdf",
  "rb": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 2 (Human)/Questions/June 2024 QP.pdf",
