  "topicConfident": true,
  "inSpec": false,
  "eq": null,
  "eqConfident": false,
  "topicCode": null,
  "topicName": null,
  "text": "Explain why some urban locations are perceived as undesirable by some groups.\n",
  "ms": "Explain why some urban locations are perceived as undesirable by some number groups.\nAO1 (6 marks)\n• Some urban locations such as London are perceived as undesirable due to high living costs particularly the high cost of housing resulting in first time buyers being unable to afford properties.\n• Some areas’ environmental quality has changed over time which can led people to view them as undesirable (industrialisation/deindustrialisation)\n• Areas with low environmental quality particularly in inner city areas where there is substandard housing, atmospheric pollution and noise and light pollution.\n• Urban locations with particularly high levels of crime and antisocial behaviour are seen to be undesirable due to concerns of over safety and wellbeing.\n• The perception of the desirability of an area depends on a range of factors, include ethnicity, age and gender, as well as the lived experience of the individual.\nAccept any other appropriate response.\nLevel Mark Descriptor\nLevel 1 0 No rewardable material.\nLevel 2 1–2\nLevel 3 • Demonstrates isolated elements of geographical knowledge and 3–4 understanding, some of which may be inaccurate or irrelevant.\n5–6 (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a narrow range of geographical ideas, which lack detail. (AO1)\n• Demonstrates geographical knowledge and understanding, which is mostly relevant and may include some inaccuracies. (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a range of geographical ideas, which are not fully detailed and/or developed. (AO1)\n• Demonstrates accurate and relevant geographical knowledge and understanding throughout. (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a broad range of geographical ideas, which are detailed and fully developed. (AO1)",
  "pageFrom": 17,
  "pageTo": 17,
  "pdf": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 2 (Human)/Questions/June 2024 QP.pdf",
  "rb": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 2 (Human)/Questions/June 2024 QP.pdf",
