  "text": "Explain the differences between colonial and neo-colonial mechanisms of\nmaintaining power.",
  "ms": "Explain the difference between colonial and neo-colonial Mark number mechanisms of maintaining power 4\nAO1 (4 marks) (4)\nAward 1 mark for identifying a key difference between colonial and neo-colonial mechanisms and a further 3 marks for expansion up to a maximum of 4 marks. For example:\n• Colonial rule always involved the transference of control (sovereignty) of territory from one group, usually the indigenous to another (the Imperial power) whereas neo- colonialism involves no such transference of sovereignty (1)\nneo-colonial ‘control’ is exercised through indirect means, not direct (1) which include political, economic and cultural mechanisms (1) example of same – e.g. Use of global institutions such as WTO or TNC’s (1)\nAccept any other appropriate response.",
  "pageFrom": 2,
  "pageTo": 2,
  "pdf": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 3 (Synoptic)/Questions/June 2020 QP.pdf",
  "rb": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 3 (Synoptic)/Resource Booklet/June 2020 RB.pdf",
