  "topicCode": null,
  "topicName": null,
  "text": "Explain why the result you have reached for the χ 2 test in 2 (a)(ii) may not be a\nreliable guide to the relationship between a country being landlocked and its\nlevel of development.",
  "ms": "(b) Explain why the result you have reached for the X2 test in 2 (a) Mark number (ii) may not be a reliable guide to the relationship between a 4 country being landlocked and its level of development.\nAO3 (4 marks) (4)\nFor each reason, award 1 mark for identifying why this result may (1+1) + not be a reliable guide to the relationship between a country being (1+1)\nlandlocked and its level of development.\nThe result is significant at the 90% level but not at 95% or 99% (1)\nso the relationship is not the strongest (possible) (1)\nThe 38 ‘land-locked’ countries may not tell the whole picture (1) if there are other countries that are land-locked not included (1)\nA statistical test such as this does not show a causal relationship\n(1) so further work would to be done to establish possible links (1)\nDefinitions of ‘development’ change and/or are arbitrary (1) so this result might change year on year (1)\nTable suggests that the distribution is quite polarised (1) which suggests need for further research (1)\nAccept any other appropriate response.",
  "pageFrom": 4,
