  "text": "Table 1 below shows the area of the northern hemisphere covered by either snow\nor ice in January and July for selected years between 1970 and 2020.\nYear Area in Rank Area in Rank d d2\nmillion km2 Order million km2 Order\nJanuary July\n1970 48.26 3 4.94 2= 0.5 0.25\n1975 44.95 11 4.60 4 7 49\n1980 45.91 9 5.40 1 8 64\n1985 50.18 1 4.94 2= –1.5 2.25\n1990 45.67 10 2.97 8 2 4\n1995 46.13 8 3.97 5 3 9\n2000 47.61 4 3.55 6= –2.5 6.25\n2005 46.56 6 3.55 6= –0.5\n2010 48.84 2 2.51 10 –8 64\n2015 47.15 5 2.52 9 –4 16\n2020 46.36 7 2.41 11 –4 16\nΣd2=\nTable 1\nComplete Table 1 by calculating the value of d2 for the year 2005 and then\ncalculating the value of Σd2\nUsing the formula below, now calculate Rs.\n§ 66d2 ·\nRs 1\u0010 ¨ 3 ¸\n©n \u0010n¹\nGive your answer to two decimal places.\nYou must show your working.\nRs = ..............................................................",
  "ms": "number (4)\nAO3 (4 marks)\nCorrect calculations of missing data 1. d2 = 0.25 (1)\n2. ∑d2 = 231 (1)\nCorrect calculation of Rs -0.05 (1)\nCorrect method Mark 231 x 6 /1386 = 1 – 1.05 = -0.05 (1)",
