  "option": null,
  "q": "4",
  "part": "",
  "marks": 8,
  "topic": "geo-syn",
  "topicConfident": true,
  "inSpec": false,
  "eq": null,
  "eqConfident": false,
  "topicCode": null,
  "topicName": null,
  "text": "Study Figure 4, Figure 5 and Figure 6 in Section A of the Resource Booklet.\nAnalyse the global implications of climate change in these polar regions.",
  "ms": "AO1 (4 marks) AO3 (4 marks)\nAO1 More significant politically, socially and economically in the Arctic because of its global location and its resident population\n• Antarctic changes are more significant environmentally in the long-term, because of contribution to sea-level rise but probably less so in the short- term\n• ..and therefore also more significant in political, economic and social long-term too Albedo effect more likely an Arctic issue given limited sea-ice changes in Antarctica Sea-level changes important consequences but Greenland data not addressed here with preoccupation on sea-ice in northern hemisphere\nAO3 Figure 4 suggests that sea-ice loss is significant in the Antarctic but\n• … very rapid in the Arctic with implications for global climate feedback mechanisms\n• Sea-ice changes maybe related to variable climate data from Figs 2 and\n• 3\n• Figure 5 shows that ice-loss from the main ice-sheet in Antarctica is very significant – 14mm of sea-level rise since 1979 at an accelerating rate Its long-term significance is enormous given the amount of water locked up Arctic ice is thin but extensive on area – thinness makes it vulnerable to temperature changes – summer ice predicted to disappear by 2100 (Figure 6)\nText references to ‘greater geopolitical significance’ of Arctic changes Accept any other appropriate response.\nLevel Mark Descriptor\nLevel 1 0 No rewardable material.\n1–3 • Demonstrates isolated elements of geographical knowledge and understanding, some of which may be inaccurate or\nLevel 2 4–6 irrelevant. (AO1)\n• Investigates the question/issue to produce a limited analysis\nLevel 3 7–8 of data/evidence, making few connections to geographical ideas. (AO3)\n• Demonstrates geographical knowledge and understanding, which is mostly relevant but may include some inaccuracies.\n(AO1)\n• Critically investigates the question/issue to produce an analysis of data/evidence, making some logical connections to geographical ideas, which are mostly relevant. (AO3)\n• Demonstrates accurate and relevant geographical knowledge and understanding throughout. (AO1)\n• Critically investigates the question/issue to produce a coherent analysis of data/evidence, making logical connections to relevant geographical ideas. (AO3)",
  "pageFrom": 6,
  "pageTo": 6,
  "pdf": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 3 (Synoptic)/Questions/June 2021 QP.pdf",
  "rb": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 3 (Synoptic)/Questions/June 2021 QP.pdf",
